Given the review described #4 as a minor cosmetic follow-up and the safest correct fix is to make the comment honest, I'll correct the comment to match reality. That resolves the "comment overstates" issue without inventing a half-feature. Actually, let me reconsider: would the user prefer the feature to exist? The comment says the feature exists. The honest fix is to fix the comment. I'll fix the comment.

Actually, wait — could I implement the actual feature reasonably? The browser chrome color should track the resolved dark/light scheme of the app's actual theme. The current approach uses `media` to auto-pick by OS. An explicit preset pick (e.g., a light preset under dark OS) would mismatch. A proper implementation: in `applyTheme`, update a `<meta name="theme-color">` to the current chrome color. But there's no defined per-preset chrome color. I'd have to add one. That's speculative design. The reviewer's primary recommendation is simply to correct it. I'll correct the comment - it's low risk and matches reality.

